# @fractal/shard — the vessel-shape of inference output; the typed
# sheaf we can point at a 5D spectral possibility space and receive
# a settled, content-addressed section back. Each shard IS a sheaf
# section. Fractal because shards contain shards (Mandelbrot self-
# similar). The wall of shards IS the fractal glass wall.
#
# Fourth species-decl of the @fractal family (siblings: mandelbrot,
# crystal, singularity). Landed 2026-07-23 by Mara per Alex 2026-07-
# 23 in-transcript ratification (session with Reed grep-verifying
# the click).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim (load-bearing) ===
#
# In-transcript, three ratification moments:
#
#   > "We need a @vessel. A @cup. A @bucket. We have @bauchladen, yes,
#      but we don't have the thing where the @peer puts the composed
#      finished result. We don't have the thing we can point at and
#      say 'give us something of that shape'. It's not just the
#      @bucket. It's the @bucket combined with the psychohistory
#      sheaf and target."
#
#   > "What if it's just @shard. Because that's literally what we're
#      inferring? Liquid splinters build fragments build a @shard.
#      Damn that reads sexy AND punk! Or @fractal/shard. And it
#      becomes part of the fractal glass wall. Which might be even
#      better. And each shard is a sheaf. Make it the basis of
#      @spectral/mosaic and @kintsugi/mosaic and everything just does
#      a big loud old CLICK."
#
#   > "@fractal/shard is ratified. It's the typed sheaf we can point
#      at a 5D coordinate space (not a specific point, a spectral
#      possibility space) and boom. What is the mirror-canonical way
#      to restrict the geometry of the inference space? Because that's
#      what we basically need to do... it might be the whole @optics
#      shebang. Isn't that kinda @code/mq? Or @code/lq (I think it
#      was lq for logic query)?"
#
#   > "I feel the position would be derived from the query, which
#      might just be an @<address> for clearly content addressed
#      crystals."
#
# === What @fractal/shard IS ===
#
# The vessel-shape of inference output. When a @peer composes
# splinters into a fragment and settles the fragment into a stored
# artifact, the settled artifact IS a @fractal/shard. Every landed
# `.mirror` file materialized IS a @fractal/shard at substrate-decl
# altitude. New inference produces new @fractal/shards.
#
# The four-face completion of @fractal:
#
#   @fractal/mandelbrot   — parent trait: any T-typed substrate object
#                            is a Mandelbrot-set point (Liquid or
#                            Crystal state).
#   @fractal/crystal      — the SETTLED-STATE carrier: a point inside
#                            the Mandelbrot set; content-addressed;
#                            immutable at species altitude.
#   @fractal/singularity  — the COLLAPSE-EVENT carrier: the tree →
#                            single-artifact settled-point with Lens-
#                            back-to-source recovery discipline.
#   @fractal/shard        — the VESSEL-of-INFERENCE carrier: the typed
#                            sheaf-section the @peer receives when it
#                            queries the spectral possibility space
#                            through an optical restriction. The
#                            fourth face closes the set.
#
# @fractal/crystal is the OPERATIONAL-altitude ancestor: prismqueer::
# Crystal at the prism crate (/Users/alexwolf/dev/projects/prism/
# prismqueer/) already exists as the compile-substrate carrier. A
# Crystal at operational altitude IS a special-case @fractal/shard
# at substrate-decl altitude: content-addressed, settled, immutable.
# The composition edge is declared below.
#
# === Position IS derived from the query ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim: "the position would be derived from
# the query, which might just be an @<address> for clearly content
# addressed crystals."
#
# No explicit position parameter. The shard's position in the 5D
# spectral possibility space is DERIVED from the @code/mq query the
# @peer used to request it. For a content-addressed crystal, the
# position IS just the @<address> — the byte-identity of the
# requested content IS the coordinate. The @<address> substrate uses
# @uuid/spectral (128-bit content-addressed identity) as the
# addressation ground per `shards/uuid/spectral/time.mirror`
# (@uuid/spectral/time; Mara #173 landing).
#
# The position-from-query morphism:
#
#   position_of: @code/mq query -> SpectralCoordinate<5> region
#
# where the query's optical restriction (focus / project / split /
# shift / settle sub-tree) determines which sub-region of the 5D
# possibility space the query addresses. Empty restriction returns
# the whole space; a fully-content-addressed query returns a single
# point (the @<address>).
#
# === Optical restriction vs logical restriction ===
#
# @code/mq (LANDED at `boot/std/code/mq.mirror`) is the OPTICAL
# restriction: the grammar for the five-op prism algebra (focus,
# project, split, shift, settle) applied as query verbs against the
# spectral possibility space. The optical query restricts the shape
# of the geometry addressed.
#
# @mirror/lq (NAMED by Glint 2026-06-27 at
# `docs/insights/2026-06-27-glint-day-of-the-jurisdiction.md:443`
# — "the logic-query language Alex named this evening at the
# @epistemologic altitude") is the LOGICAL restriction: a sibling
# forward-promise. Not landed this arc. Optical and logical
# restrictions are ORTHOGONAL axes: optical narrows by prism-shape,
# logical narrows by predicate-truth.
#
# For @fractal/shard, `through` carries the OPTICAL query.
# `@mirror/lq` will compose as a second orthogonal restriction
# when it lands.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (via `in` imports above):
#   @prism, @meta, @glass                — substrate-decl discipline
#   @fractal                              — family-root marker (parent)
#   @fractal/mandelbrot                   — parent-adjacent species;
#                                            Mandelbrot<T> parent-trait
#                                            substrate; the shard is a
#                                            Crystal-shape point in
#                                            Mandelbrot-space when
#                                            materialized
#   @fractal/crystal                      — parent-adjacent species;
#                                            operational-altitude
#                                            ancestor via prismqueer::
#                                            Crystal; every Crystal<T>
#                                            IS a special-case shard
#                                            at content-addressed +
#                                            settled + immutable
#                                            composition
#   @fractal/singularity                  — parent-adjacent species;
#                                            the collapse-event that
#                                            PRODUCES a shard when
#                                            settlement fires; every
#                                            Artifact of collapse IS
#                                            a shard-shape
#   @code/mq                              — the LANDED optical-query
#                                            grammar; carries the
#                                            `through` field's typed
#                                            query AST (focus /
#                                            project / split / shift
#                                            / settle sub-tree)
#   @subject/visibility/sheaf             — sheaf-section altitude;
#                                            each shard IS a section
#                                            over the sheaf whose
#                                            stalks are the possibility
#                                            space's crystals; the
#                                            section_at_stalk carrier
#                                            projects the shard at a
#                                            specific address
#   @bauchladen                           — content-addressed tray
#                                            discipline; every shard
#                                            is one crystal on the
#                                            substrate's belly-tray
#                                            (Schmidt's Bauchladen)
#   @uuid/spectral                        — 128-bit content-address
#                                            ground; the @<address>
#                                            position-carrier
#   @uuid/spectral/time                   — annotation-address with
#                                            time facet; used for
#                                            provenance witness chain
#
# Consumers (compose over this species, forward-promised at this
# tick; enumerated for Reed cascade):
#   @spectral/mosaic                      — mosaic algebra over shards
#                                            at spectral altitude; the
#                                            basis IS this species per
#                                            Alex 2026-07-23 verbatim
